==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Dark Catman''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Ultimate Catman''' level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

Evolves into '''Catman Forever''' at level 60 using [[Catfruit#Behemoth Stones|Behemoth Stones]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Catman is a generalist in many regards. He packs a punch even against enemies outside of his niche, he has great survivability, and he stays almost as far back as [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]]. This may be further hindered by his somewhat long attack cycle, foreswing and rather high cost, but he still remains a great choice in every part of the game, and this strength gets amplified when he faces his targeted traits.

Catman's first three forms possess the same stats and the Massive Damage ability against [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Aliens]], though they also target an additional trait that varies between forms. For most of [[Into the Future]], [[Cats of the Cosmos]] and [[Stories of Legend]], Catman can easily take down his targets with little issue, but shouldn't be used for threats that outrange him as he will be unlikely to land enough attacks to be worth his cost and his long cooldown makes it difficult to recover if he is destroyed early.

==='''Normal Form'''===
Catman's Normal Form is the one you will probably use the most due to [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] being such a common trait, along with him carrying the same [[:Category:Anti-Alien Cats|anti-Alien]] ability present in all forms. This form gives him plenty of targets to outrange, including [[Owlbrow]] and most variants of [[The Face]], [[Teacher Bun Bun]] and [[Mooth]], among others.

==='''Evolved Form'''===
Dark Catman changes his secondary target to [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angels]], of which he outranges a decent amount. Dark Catman can bring the hurt to anything up to and including [[Angelic Sleipnir]], [[Winged Pigge]], and even [[Youcan]] and [[St. Dober]] if frozen. While he is overall harder to use against Angels than against other traits, this form shouldn't be disregarded, as Dark Catman can still help out tons, and given that a decent chunk of Floating enemies are also Aliens, he doesn't lose too much, and gains a great trade off.

==='''True Form'''===
Ultimate Catman changes his secondary target to [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relics]] and gains Curse Immunity. The targeting change is a mixed bag as while he is very effective at nuking short- to mid-ranged Relics like [[Oldhorn]], [[M. Ost]], [[Relic Bun-Bun]], and even [[Mr. Puffington]] provided a good setup, the likes of [[Loris]], [[Lowkey]], and [[Othom]] can easily render him useless. This True Form evolution also doesn't come cheap due to requiring 2 Elder [[Catfruit]] and facing competition from other [[:Category:Anti-Relic Cats|anti-Relic specialists]] that have better utility elsewhere. Still, Ultimate Catman may be worth the investment if alternatives are not available.

==='''Ultra Form'''===
Off rip, Catman Forever reduces his attack cycle by 33%, which is effectively a 50% DPS boost compared to his previous forms. Becoming a rebound attacker is mostly beneficial to a backline nuker like him, since it prevents him from clipping into enemies with his moderately high speed. However, he is very prone to getting distracted, sometimes repeatedly wasting his 6-second attack animation on nothing if peons continually intercept him.

Catman Forever regains the Angel targeting from his Evolved Form. Given the sheer power of his attacks at Lv.60, he actually has a good matchup into the entire trait as a whole. He outranges almost every common Angel, and, despite lacking any immunities, can handle piercers like Youcan, [[Angelic Beast Rajakong]], and St. Dober with the right strategy. Even against non-targets in mixed stages, his base damage is more than good enough to justify bringing him along just to nuke one troublesome target out of existence.

[[Immune to Drain|Drain Immunity]]'s most notable application is in [[Endless Forms Most Beautiful]], where [[Sage of Selection Darvin]] can no longer cut his cooldown. He completely hard-counters the stage as a result, seeing how he targets every relevant threat there. If you're struggling on that particular [[:Category:Mythic Bosses|Mythic Boss]] stage, it may be worth unlocking Catman Forever to make things a whole lot easier.

==='''Talents'''===
The '''[[Dodge Attack]]''' Talent is a good answer to enemies that can pierce, although somewhat unreliable. In his Ultra Form, Catman can take advantage of the HP boost to keep himself alive far longer than he would otherwise.

'''[[Immune to Warp]]''' is a situational Talent, reminiscent of [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]]'s Immune to Warp Talent. While it can help against [[:Category:Starred Alien Enemies|Starred Aliens]], it also risks reducing his survivability by a lot in stages, especially against high-magnification [[Star Peng]]s or [[Mesocosmocyclone]]s.

'''[[Immune to Freeze]]''' is a nice talent to have against stages with [[Henry]], but is also very expensive for what it does, as he can avoid many [[:Category:Enemies with Freeze ability|Freezing enemies]] of his targeted traits like [[Maawth]] and [[I.M. Phace]] with his range, and better options exist for those he cannot outrange, as a mere Immunity to Freeze will not prevent him from being whittled down from afar.

As Catman mainly serves as a nuker, '''Attack Buff''' is nice to have. '''HP Buff''', on the other hand, doesn't serve much of a purpose due to him relying on his range to keep himself safe.

